--TEST--
A `Core\Env::secret` value reaches no output sink, and its name refuses a `tainted` argument — `rule:security/secret-sinks-refuse`, `rule:security/sink-predicate`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The answer is `secret`, so `echo` and a log record refuse it as they refuse
// every other `secret` value. The name is a sink as `get`'s is: a request that
// chose it would choose which credential the program reads.
var $key = Core\Env::secret("NVS_CASE_API_KEY") ?? "";
echo $key, "\n";
Core\Log::write(Core\Log::Level::Info, "loaded", ["key" => $key]);

tainted string $chosen = "NVS_CASE_API_KEY";
var $leak = Core\Env::secret($chosen);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0790]: `echo` cannot print a `secret` value
  --> case.nvs:6:6
%A
error[E0797]: a `secret`-qualified value cannot be written to a log record; a log is read by a person and kept by a pipeline, so the value would be disclosed rather than used
  --> case.nvs:7:60
%A
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `tainted string`
   --> case.nvs:10:30
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
